  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no earlier ticket that reports this problem. I searched on TestListFilesEnvVar, RunPageTests, RunListPage, ParseCommandline and the assertion text. The only Run-extension tickets were PowerToys#48595 and #48445, and both are runtime crashes in the Run commands extension, not a flaky unit test. This looks like a new test-stability issue. The test's IRunHistoryService mock calls the real RunHistory.ParseCommandline, which can take longer than RunListPage's 200 ms parsing deadline on a slow CI machine. When it does, the page returns no items. The fix is to make the mock return a deterministic result instead of calling the real parser, or to make the deadline injectable so the test can use a longer one.\"}",
